cial work characteristics and self rated health in four post-communist countries</article-title><source>J Epidemiol Community Health</source><year>2001</year><volume>55</volume><fpage>624</fpage><lpage>630</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11511640</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/jech.55.9.624</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stansfeld</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Bosma</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Hemingway</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Marmot</surname><given-names>MG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Psychosocial work characteristics and social support as predictors of SF-36 health functioning: The Whitehall II study</article-title><source>Psychosom Med</source><year>1998</year><volume>60</volume><fpage>247</fpage><lpage>255</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9625210</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>de Jonge</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Bosma</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Peter</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Siegrist</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Job strain, effort-reward imbalance and employee well-being: A large-scale cross-sectional study</article-title><source>Soc Sci Med</source><year>2000</year><volume>50</volume><fpage>1317</fpage><lpage>1327</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10728851</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0277-9536(99)00388-3</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pikhart</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Bobak</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Pajak</surname><given-na